            <div class="cfs-prose legal">

<div class="notice-box">
                <p>This Privacy Policy explains how CertiFried MultiTool collects, uses, stores, and protects your information when you use our Discord bot, the dashboard, the stream bot (including song requests), the CertiFried Studio app for Windows, and Greenhouse Tycoon. <a href="/legal/data">Data we collect</a> gives the same information as tables, product by product.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="introduction">1. Introduction</h2>
                <p>At CertiFried MultiTool, we are committed to protecting your privacy. We only collect the minimum data necessary to provide our services and never sell your information to third parties.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="information-we-collect">2. Information We Collect</h2>
                <h3>Automatically Collected Data</h3>
                <div class="cfs-table-wrap"><table class="data-table">
                    <thead><tr><th>Data Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Retention</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><strong>Discord User ID</strong></td><td>Identify users for features</td><td>Until deletion request</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><strong>Discord Server ID</strong></td><td>Store server configurations</td><td>Until bot removal</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><strong>Username</strong></td><td>Display in commands/leaderboards</td><td>Cached temporarily</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><strong>Channel & Role IDs</strong></td><td>Configure features</td><td>Until changed</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table></div>
                <h3>User-Provided Data</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Streamer tracking preferences and platform usernames (Twitch, Kick, YouTube, Rumble, TikTok) and social feed subscriptions (YouTube, Twitter/X, Bluesky, TikTok videos, RSS)</li>
                    <li>Custom command and custom embed configurations, and the values a server's custom commands save for you or for the server (<code>{db:…}</code> and <code>{sdb:…}</code> storage)</li>
                    <li>Economy, leveling, gambling, trading, and pet data (currency balances, inventories, shop purchases)</li>
                    <li>Game progress and stats: Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5e RPG character data (characters, inventory, combat and quest progress), word-game and Cards Against Humanity scores, trivia, hangman, and counting stats</li>
                    <li>Form responses, ticket messages, and support interactions, including Stream Team application form responses</li>
                    <li>Moderation logs, warnings, and infraction history</li>
                    <li>Voice transcripts, in servers whose staff turn on voice transcription: the text of what each speaker said, with their user ID and display name</li>
                    <li>If you connect your Twitch channel to the dashboard: your channel's stream statistics, chatter lists, moderator actions, held AutoMod messages, Bits and raids, and, only if you turn on chat sampling, the text of chat messages</li>
                    <li>Birthday dates and birthday card signatures, messages, likes, and replies</li>
                    <li>Reaction role selections</li>
                    <li>Welcome card and appearance customizations (uploaded images)</li>
                    <li>Suggestion, poll, and giveaway participation</li>
                    <li>Anonymous confessions you send, and, privately for 30 days, the fact that you sent them</li>
                    <li>Custom bot tokens (encrypted with AES-256-GCM at rest)</li>
                    <li>Per-user Buy Me a Coffee API keys you link for supporter announcements (encrypted at rest)</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Group Greeting Cards Data</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Card data:</strong> Card title, occasion type, recipient name, creator name, background images (including AI-generated), music URLs, wishlist links, logos, passwords (hashed with SHA-256), scheduled delivery dates</li>
                    <li><strong>Signature data:</strong> Signer name, Discord/Twitch user ID (if logged in), avatar URL, message text, custom font settings (color, family, size), GIF/image URLs, YouTube video URLs</li>
                    <li><strong>Voice recordings:</strong> Audio files (WebM format, max 30 seconds) recorded via browser MediaRecorder API, stored as files on our server</li>
                    <li><strong>Gift card codes:</strong> Encrypted with AES-256-GCM before storage. The plaintext code exists only briefly in server memory during encryption/decryption. Codes are never logged, never rendered in HTML, and never accessible to administrators</li>
                    <li><strong>Guest signer data:</strong> Name and optional email address provided by the guest. No account is created. Guest entries are identified by a random ID (not trackable across cards)</li>
                    <li><strong>AI image prompts:</strong> Text prompts used to generate card covers are stored alongside the card for reference. Prompts are sent to Google&rsquo;s Gemini API for image generation, or to Hugging Face&rsquo;s image service when Gemini cannot make the image</li>
                    <li><strong>Likes, replies, and view counts:</strong> Signature likes, threaded replies, and page view counts</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Dashboard Data</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Discord OAuth session data (user ID, username, guild list) for dashboard authentication</li>
                    <li>Session IP address and user agent (for security monitoring)</li>
                    <li>Uploaded files (avatars, welcome banners, PDF imports, voice recordings, AI-generated images) stored on the server</li>
                </ul>
                <h3 id="greenhouse-tycoon">Greenhouse Tycoon (website game, Twitch panel and Discord)</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Account:</strong> the platforms you sign in with (Discord, Twitch or Kick), your user ID and display name on each, and the name you play under. Discord sign-in uses your dashboard login; Twitch and Kick sign-in only read your basic profile. If you link your sign-ins, they share one save.</li>
                    <li><strong>Twitch panel:</strong> Twitch gives every extension an anonymous viewer ID. The panel only receives your real Twitch user ID if you choose to share it, so your greenhouse is kept between streams and matches the website. You can revoke this in Twitch&rsquo;s settings at any time.</li>
                    <li><strong>Game progress:</strong> in-game cash and items, your plants and the hybrids you bred, upgrades and staff, quests, achievements, decorations and badges, season standings, notifications, and when you last played.</li>
                    <li><strong>Records the game keeps to work fairly:</strong> every change to your cash and items, daily reward claims, and when sign-ins were linked or unlinked (so a reward or starter kit cannot be claimed twice).</li>
                    <li><strong>On your device:</strong> the website keeps a sign-in token in your browser&rsquo;s local storage. Signing out removes it. The Twitch panel stores nothing on your device.</li>
                    <li>The game has no purchases. It does not use Bits, subscriptions or payment details.</li>
                    <li><strong>Your data:</strong> on the website, the <strong>Your data</strong> card in the game&rsquo;s Profile lets you download a copy of your save or delete it, whichever platform you sign in with (see Your Rights below).</li>
                    <li><strong>The old game:</strong> Greenhouse Tycoon replaces CertiFried Tycoon, the earlier game on this site, which is closed. Nothing carries over from it. Its data was deleted from our database on November 19, 2026; one offline backup, kept only in case the change had to be undone, is deleted on February 17, 2027.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3 id="activities">Discord Activities (Watch Together and Greenhouse Tycoon in Discord)</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Signing in:</strong> the first time you open CertiFried&rsquo;s Activity, Discord asks you to share your basic profile: your user ID, username, display name and avatar. We use it to know who you are in the Activity and who hosts. Discord&rsquo;s access token is handed back to the Activity once and not stored. Discord also tells us which voice channel the Activity runs in and who is connected, which we check and do not keep.</li>
                    <li><strong>Watch Together:</strong> for each session we keep the server, the voice channel, the Activity&rsquo;s ID, who hosted, the title playing, the position and the queue, so a film carries on if our server restarts. Who is watching right now, and whether their video is still loading, is held in memory only and shown to the others in the session with your name and avatar.</li>
                    <li><strong>Video:</strong> films come from the CertiFried film library (a Jellyfin server) and are streamed through our server. Requests from the Activity reach us through Discord&rsquo;s proxy, which does not pass your IP address on. The Activity remembers your volume in its local storage in your Discord app.</li>
                    <li><strong>Greenhouse Tycoon in Discord</strong> is the same game and the same save as signing in with Discord on the website (see above).</li>
                    <li>What a server plays is that server&rsquo;s responsibility; servers should only show what they have the right to show.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3 id="stream-bot-data">Stream bot (your own Twitch, Kick and YouTube channels)</h3>
                <p>The stream bot belongs to your CertiFried account, not to a Discord server. If you use it, we keep:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Profile and channels:</strong> your settings, the Twitch, Kick and YouTube channels you linked, and the Discord channels you chose for posts.</li>
                    <li><strong>Twitch Stream bot grant:</strong> access and refresh tokens and the permissions you approved, encrypted. The grant never asks for the list of channels you follow or for your earnings.</li>
                    <li><strong>Tip services:</strong> which services you connected (StreamElements, Streamlabs, Ko-fi, Buy Me a Coffee, Throne, Fourthwall) and, for StreamElements and Streamlabs, your token, encrypted. We only receive notifications of tips, memberships and orders; CertiFried never processes a payment and never sees payment details.</li>
                    <li><strong>Event log:</strong> follows, subs, cheers, raids, channel point redemptions, polls, tips, OBS events and voice command phrases, each with the viewer&rsquo;s platform ID, login and display name where there is one, the amount and the message, and the notification as the platform sent it (up to 16 KB). Chat messages are only kept if you turn on <strong>Keep chat in the event log</strong>; otherwise chat runs your automations and is not stored.</li>
                    <li><strong>Your setup:</strong> automations, timers, counters and stored values, sounds you upload, overlay settings and the images and videos you upload for alerts, and the reports of Firebot or Streamer.bot imports (passwords and tokens are removed before anything is stored).</li>
                    <li><strong>Run history</strong> (what each automation did) and the actions sent to CertiFried Studio and overlays, with their results.</li>
                    <li><strong>Viewer records</strong> (the Viewers tab): for each viewer of your channels, their platform ID, login and display name, first and last seen, watch time, chat message count, points, rank, the follows, subs, gift subs, Bits, raids and tips that came from them (counts and amounts as notified; CertiFried never handles money), and a history of point changes. Watch time is counted every 5 minutes while you are live: on Twitch from the list of people in your chat (the Stream bot grant&rsquo;s chatters permission), on Kick, which offers no such list, from who chatted in the last 10 minutes.</li>
                    <li id="youtube-api"><strong>YouTube (when you link it):</strong> your Google sign-in for the channel (access and refresh tokens and the one permission asked for, to manage your YouTube chat), encrypted; the current broadcast and where the chat reader got to, so a restart carries on; and how many YouTube API units your channel used each day (kept 30 days). CertiFried uses YouTube API Services to find your live broadcast and read and act in its chat: linking YouTube means you agree to the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>, and Google&rsquo;s handling of your data is covered by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>. You can remove CertiFried&rsquo;s access at any time on <a href="https://security.google.com/settings/security/permissions" rel="noopener">Google&rsquo;s security settings page</a>; unlinking the channel on Connections also revokes it, and <code>/privacy delete</code> deletes our copy.</li>
                    <li><strong>Paired devices:</strong> each device&rsquo;s name, app version, what it can do, when it was last seen, and a SHA-256 hash of its token (never the token itself).</li>
                </ul>
                <h3 id="viewer-data">Viewers in a streamer&rsquo;s channel</h3>
                <p>If you chat, follow, cheer, tip or request songs in the channel of a streamer who uses the stream bot, that streamer&rsquo;s stream bot records the event with your platform ID, login and display name, and what you typed for a song request. It also keeps a viewer record for you in that channel: when you were first and last seen, how long you watched, how many chat messages you sent, your points and rank, and how many follows, subs, gift subs, Bits, raids and tips came from you. On YouTube that includes your Super Chats, Super Stickers, Jewels gifts and memberships, as YouTube notified them (CertiFried never handles money). The streamer can see it. Someone else&rsquo;s event can also name you: a chat reply to you or an @mention (where the streamer keeps chat), a gift sub you received, or a raid into your channel. Exports include those, and deleting your data removes your name and ID from them while the other person&rsquo;s event stays. You can export or delete it with <code>/privacy</code> if your Twitch, Kick or YouTube account is linked to CertiFried, or without an account on <a href="/privacy/viewer">Your viewer data</a>; otherwise email us (see Contact below).</p>
                <h3 id="song-requests">Song requests</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>A request stores who asked (platform ID, login and display name), what they typed, the song found and what happened to it. A viewer&rsquo;s <code>!like</code> is stored too.</li>
                    <li>To find a song, the text typed is looked up in Spotify&rsquo;s catalogue with CertiFried&rsquo;s own Spotify app (no user account is involved) and on YouTube and YouTube Music through our own resolvers; SoundCloud and YouTube links are read directly. The audio is streamed from our server to the streamer&rsquo;s OBS.</li>
                    <li>A streamer who linked their own Spotify can choose to play requests with it (off by default); that uses their linked Spotify session.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3 id="certifried-studio">CertiFried Studio (the Windows app)</h3>
                <p>Studio keeps its settings, encrypted secrets and logs on your PC. It sends CertiFried the names of your OBS scenes, sources, audio sources and filters and of your sounds, OBS events, recognised voice command phrases and the results of actions. Microphone audio and your OBS password never leave your PC, and Studio contains no analytics, telemetry or crash reporting. The full list, checked against the app&rsquo;s code, is on <a href="/studio/privacy">Studio privacy</a>.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="how-we-use-your-information">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Deliver bot features and process commands</li>
                    <li>Send stream notifications and announcements</li>
                    <li>Manage economy, leveling, and game systems</li>
                    <li>Run Greenhouse Tycoon: your greenhouse and progress, seasons, weekly challenges and leaderboards</li>
                    <li>Run your stream bot: automations, chat replies, timers, song requests, and the actions CertiFried Studio carries out on your PC</li>
                    <li>Provide moderation and security tools</li>
                    <li>Analyze usage patterns to improve features (from our own records; we use no third-party analytics or advertising)</li>
                    <li>Prevent abuse and enforce Terms of Service</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="administrator-access-disclosure">Administrator Access Disclosure</h2>
                <p>In the interest of full transparency, the following authorized administrators have dashboard access to view guild settings and bot configurations for any server with the bot installed:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>xXDeath420Xx</strong> (Discord ID: 365905620060340224) &mdash; Lead Developer &amp; Bot Owner</li>
                    <li><strong>Orsokuma (Bear)</strong> (Discord ID: 685127470625980501) &mdash; Co-Administrator &amp; Support Lead</li>
                </ul>
                <p>This access is used <strong>exclusively for bot support purposes</strong> &mdash; diagnosing issues, verifying configurations, and assisting server administrators. We will never access, manage, or modify your server settings without your explicit consent and knowledge.</p>
                <p>Administrator access does <strong>not</strong> include reading private messages, accessing restricted channels, or viewing any user's Discord authentication credentials.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="information-sharing">4. Information Sharing</h2>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    We will NEVER sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third parties.
                </div>
                <p>Some game information is visible to other players by design: Greenhouse Tycoon leaderboards and season results show the name you play under, your level, your Replant count and your season score, and a server's admins can see on the dashboard which of their members play with Discord.</p>
                <p>We integrate with third-party APIs (Discord, Twitch, Kick, YouTube, TikTok, Rumble, Bluesky, X through FxTwitter, SoundCloud, Spotify, Steam, Buy Me a Coffee, Throne, Fourthwall and Ko-fi) to provide features. Weather commands send the place or ZIP code you give to Open-Meteo, Zippopotam.us and the US National Weather Service. Lookup and fun commands (dictionary, game prices, movies, GIFs and the like) send only what you type to the service that answers them. These services have their own privacy policies.</p>
                <p>AI features (AI chat replies, the D&amp;D Dungeon Master, generated card covers and schedule images) send the text you give them to Google&rsquo;s Gemini API. Generated images go to Hugging Face&rsquo;s image service instead when Gemini cannot make them. Some AI replies run on language models on our own servers first, and voice transcription runs only on our own servers: that audio is never sent to a third party or stored (the transcript text is kept as described under Data Retention).</p>
                <p>For the stream bot, we call Twitch, Kick and YouTube on your behalf with the permissions you gave (reading your channel&rsquo;s events, sending chat, changing your title or category, making clips and the like), and connect to StreamElements or Streamlabs with your token to receive tip notifications. Song lookups send what was typed to Spotify (catalogue search only), YouTube and SoundCloud, as described above. Twitch, Kick, OBS, Spotify, YouTube, SoundCloud and the tip services each have their own privacy policies.</p>
                <p>Our website and its connections (including CertiFried Studio&rsquo;s) are served through Cloudflare, which processes visitors&rsquo; IP addresses and request details to deliver and protect the site.</p>
                <p>CertiFried&rsquo;s Discord Activities run inside Discord, which delivers them through its own Activity proxy (discordsays.com); Discord&rsquo;s privacy policy covers that.</p>
                <p>We may disclose information if required by law.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="data-security">5. Data Security</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Transport Encryption:</strong> All data in transit uses TLS/SSL</li>
                    <li><strong>At-Rest Encryption:</strong> Sensitive data (custom bot tokens, gift card codes) is encrypted with AES-256-GCM using a server-side encryption key</li>
                    <li><strong>Password Hashing:</strong> Card passwords and user authentication tokens are hashed with SHA-256 (one-way, non-reversible)</li>
                    <li><strong>Database Security:</strong> Password-protected with restricted access, private network only</li>
                    <li><strong>Stream bot secrets:</strong> device tokens and pairing codes are stored only as SHA-256 hashes; Twitch grant tokens and tip-service tokens are encrypted with AES-256-GCM and are never shown or exported</li>
                    <li><strong>Gift Code Isolation:</strong> Encrypted gift card codes are never rendered in page HTML, never logged, and only decryptable through a signed-in request by the card's recipient or its creator</li>
                    <li><strong>Rate Limiting:</strong> Protection against abuse on all API endpoints</li>
                    <li><strong>Regular Updates:</strong> Security patches applied promptly</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="where-data-is-kept">Where Your Data Is Kept</h2>
                <p>CertiFried&rsquo;s servers and database are hosted in the United Kingdom. Our website and its connections are delivered through Cloudflare&rsquo;s global network (a content delivery network), so a request may pass through a Cloudflare data centre near you before it reaches our servers. The services we connect to for you (Discord, Twitch, Kick, Google Gemini and the others named under Information Sharing) handle data in their own locations under their own policies.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="data-retention">6. Data Retention</h2>
                <div class="cfs-table-wrap"><table class="data-table">
                    <thead><tr><th>Data Category</th><th>Retention Period</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>Server configurations</td><td>Until bot removal</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>User economy/leveling data</td><td>Until deletion request</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Moderation &amp; audit logs</td><td>365 days (each server can choose a shorter period)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Moderation records (warnings, infractions, bans)</td><td>Warnings are deleted after one year. Other records (bans, kicks, mutes and the like) are deleted after two years, so moderators can see repeat offences meanwhile; that server's staff can remove them sooner. Not removed by <code>/privacy delete</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Support tickets (form answers, staff notes) and their transcripts</td><td>365 days after the ticket is closed; an open ticket is kept while it is open. Not removed by <code>/privacy delete</code>: ask that server's staff</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Modmail conversations (the messages you and a server's staff sent through the bot)</td><td>365 days after the conversation is closed; an open conversation is kept while it is open. Not removed by <code>/privacy delete</code>: ask that server's staff</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Raid lockdown records (when a lockdown ran and which accounts it kept out)</td><td>180 days after the lockdown ends</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Server join history (when you joined each server)</td><td>Kept indefinitely so a server's rejoin limit can count past joins; that server's staff can reset your count. Not removed by <code>/privacy delete</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Command usage (which command you ran, in which server and channel, when, and whether it worked)</td><td>400 days, then deleted; removed by <code>/privacy delete</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Daily command totals per server (no user IDs)</td><td>Kept indefinitely</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Cached message copies (for deleted/edited message logs)</td><td>90 days (each server can choose a shorter period); none at all if you use <code>/privacy opt-out</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Images from deleted messages (servers that turn on evidence capture)</td><td>Private copy for up to 72 hours; if the message is deleted, re-posted to that server's evidence channel</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Activity statistics</td><td>180 days</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Invite tracking (which invite you joined a server with)</td><td>180 days</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Voice transcripts (servers that turn on voice transcription)</td><td>30 days, or the period that server sets (1 to 365 days); your own lines are removed by <code>/privacy delete</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Roles kept for members who leave (servers that turn on sticky roles)</td><td>30 days after you leave, or the period that server sets (1 to 365 days)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Values custom commands save (<code>{db:…}</code> for you, <code>{sdb:…}</code> for a server)</td><td>Deleted after 400 days without being read or written; yours are removed by <code>/privacy delete</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td>AI chat memory (recent messages the AI reply feature uses as context)</td><td>24 hours</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Who sent an anonymous confession</td><td>Stored privately for 30 days, then deleted. Members never see it; that server's admins can reveal it from the dashboard, and every reveal is logged. Not removed by <code>/privacy delete</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Stream announcements</td><td>Deleted when stream ends (configurable)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Stream history of tracked streamers (when each stream started and ended)</td><td>730 days</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Twitch channel statistics for channels connected to the dashboard (per-minute stream and chatter snapshots, sampled chat text)</td><td>90 days</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Twitch moderator actions and held AutoMod messages for connected channels</td><td>180 days</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Twitch Bits and raids for connected channels</td><td>365 days</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Birthday cards &amp; signatures</td><td>Indefinite (deletable by card creator or admin)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Standalone greeting cards</td><td>Indefinite (deletable by card creator)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Voice recordings</td><td>Deleted with the associated signature or card (the audio file within a day); a recording never added to a signature is deleted after a day</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Encrypted gift card codes</td><td>Deleted with the associated signature or card</td></tr>
